window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>I've spent the better part of a decade trying to save the world.</b></p> <p>Twice a century, Mount Slate threatens to erupt, and for my entire life, the four families in charge haven't seemed to care about their impending doom.</p> <p>So it fell to me to try to fix things. To make peace.</p> <p>Me, a man whose greatest skill is pissing people off so much that they challenge me to a duel, and then killing them in that duel.</p> <p>Now the moment is here, and my clever stone is telling me that one man—a sweet, innocent, infuriating judgmental bastard—is the only one who's capable of saving the world. And I have to help him do it.</p> <p>I'm starting to wonder if the world is even worth saving.</p> <p>Moonstriker <i>is the last in a series of four books, starring one cynical not-quite-assassin, one ray of sunshine, and one very grumpy mountain. It features both Aubrey and Kit's HEA, as well as the conclusion of the overall series arc.</i></p>"; 
